SOAPBOX: Personal best for this Little Pistol. Even worked DXCC-In-A-Contest for
SOAPBOX: the first time ever with 107 unique DXC in the log. 40m was the most
SOAPBOX: fun. DX was loud and plenty-full on 40m both nights. Saturday night
SOAPBOX: was the best though. Rolled out of bed just B4 sunrise Sunday morning
SOAPBOX: to test my luck on 40m to Asia and PAC and wasn't disappointed. 40m
SOAPBOX: was a rock star! Good openings to Asia and PAC on 10 and 15 Saturday late
SOAPBOX: afternoon and early evening. VK9DX was as loud on 40m early Sunday morning
SOAPBOX: as he was on 10m Satuday early evening! Lots of fun chasing mults and DX
SOAPBOX: around the bands.
SOAPBOX: One thing that would make CQWW DX contests even more exciting would be the
SOAPBOX: addition of a single element wires/verticals category. TB/Wires will always
SOAPBOX: out perform the simple single element stations. There are lots of us out here!
SOAPBOX: It would be nice to be able to compete against similar stations for awards.
SOAPBOX: I would be first in line to sponsor a plaque/s for this category.
SOAPBOX: Think about it...sereously please...
SOAPBOX: 73, Gene N9TF K3S 100 watts to 6BTV ground mounted, or, 160m inverted L 22'
SOAPBOX: vertical to knee.
